Implement Agentwork Workflow logic within compliance_agent. Agent Workflow logic is mentioned below
Create Bigquery and GCS tools within compliancel_agent.
Grounding: Troubleshooting_pca_continuous_monitoring.pdf should be copied to gs://impact_compliance-1 and used for grounding some of the information
BigQuery dataset:Project ID: customers-444618 BIGQUERY_DATASET_ID="compliance_agent" most of tables have suffix _20251106 below queries not added suffix. Please make sure to add suffixes wherever required.
Model Selection: gemini-3.6-flash

Agent Workflow:
Step0: Input: publisher_ID (e.g., 4381629). Optionally, a JIRA_ticket_ID (e.g., IRFRAUD-8254) can be used for context in the final summary.


Step 1: Identify Linked Accounts
Action: Execute the BigQuery query to find all accounts within the same graph_id as the input publisher_ID.
Query:
WITH graph AS (
  SELECT graph_id
  FROM customers-444618.compliance_agent.account_graph_main_20251106
  WHERE account_id = 2020202
)
SELECT DISTINCT ag.Account_id
FROM customers-444618.compliance_agent.account_graph_main_20251106 ag
JOIN graph g ON ag.graph_id = g.graph_id;
Output: A list of unique account_ids, referred to as account_list.
Step 2-4: Parallel Data Extraction for all accounts in account_list
The agent will execute the queries from Steps 2, 3, and 4 in parallel for all IDs in account_list.

Step 2: Get Publisher Summary & Top Programs
Query 2.1 (Publisher Details):
SELECT publisher_id, publisher_name, publisher_description, primary_promo_method, company_url, country, account_status, account_creation_date, marketplace_status, marketplace_approval_date, publisher_rating, is_qualified_to_pay, lifetime_gtv, last_30_day_day_gtv, Top1_ref_domain, partnership_count
FROM `customers-444618.compliance_agent.publisher`
WHERE publisher_id IN UNNEST(@account_list);
Query 2.2 (Top Programs):
WITH raw AS (
  SELECT publisher_id, program_name, lifetime_gtv,
  ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY publisher_id ORDER BY lifetime_gtv DESC) AS gtv_rank
  FROM `customers-444618.compliance_agent.partnership_affiliation`
  WHERE publisher_id IN UNNEST(@account_list)
)
SELECT publisher_id, STRING_AGG(program_name ORDER BY gtv_rank LIMIT 10) as top_programs
FROM raw
WHERE gtv_rank <= 10
GROUP BY 1;

Step 3: Marketplace Approval History
Query 3:
SELECT publisher_id, request_context__title as publisher_name, TIMESTAMP(application_evaluation_date) as application_date, result_state as evaluation,
       TRIM(CONCAT(
         IF(evaluations__profanity_check__result = "FAILED", "profanity,", ""),
         IF(evaluations__duplicate_device_id__result = "FAILED", "duplicate_device,", ""),
         IF(evaluations__unique_media_properties__result = "FAILED", "non_unique_media_property,", ""),
         IF(evaluations__email_domain__result = "FAILED", "high_risk_email_domain,", ""),
         IF(evaluations__email_risk__result = "FAILED", "high_risk_email,", ""),
         IF(evaluations__ip_risk__result = "FAILED", "high_risk_ip,", ""),
         IF(evaluations__url_risk__result = "FAILED", "high_risk_url,", ""),
         IF(evaluations__geo_risk__result = "FAILED", "high_risk_geo,", ""),
         IF(evaluations__fake_audience__result = "FAILED", "fake_audience,", ""),
         IF(evaluations__offensive_text__result = "FAILED", "offensive_text,", ""),
         IF(evaluations__offensive_image__result = "FAILED", "offensive_image", "")
       ), ',') as decline_reasons
FROM `customers-444618.compliance_agent.rtas_results`
WHERE publisher_id IN UNNEST(@account_list)
UNION ALL
SELECT id as publisher_id, organizationname as publisher_name, TIMESTAMP(platform_application_date) as application_date, prediction as evaluation, decline_reasons
FROM `customers-444618.compliance_agent.iram_application_scored`
WHERE id IN UNNEST(@account_list);

Step 4: Compliance History (JIRA)
Query 4:
SELECT r.issue_id, r.partner_id, r.created_date, r.summary, r.description, r.status, c.status_changed, c.author as commenter, c.body as comment, c.created as comment_created
FROM `customers-444618.compliance_agent.raw_data` r
LEFT JOIN `customers-444618.compliance_agent.comments` c ON r.issue_id = c.issue
WHERE EXISTS (
  SELECT 1
  FROM UNNEST(SPLIT(r.partner_id, " ")) pid
  WHERE SAFE_CAST(REGEXP_EXTRACT(pid, "[0-9]+") AS INT64) IN UNNEST(@account_list)
);

Step 5: Initial Publisher Risk Analysis (7, 30, 365-day intervals)
Action: Execute the provided query three times, substituting @date_interval with 7, 30, and 365. These can be run in parallel.
Query 5 (Template):
SELECT publisher_id, publisher_name, IF(publisher_id = @publisher_ID, 1, 0) as primary,
       AVG(Actions_7days) as avg_weekly_actions, AVG(Clicks_7days) as avg_weekly_clicks, AVG(Commissions_7days) as avg_weekly_commissions,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(Long_cta_pct * actions_7days), SUM(actions_7days)) as long_cta_pct,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(Injected_click_pct * actions_7days), SUM(actions_7days)) as Injected_click_pct,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(Click_spamming_pct * actions_7days), SUM(actions_7days)) as Click_spamming_pct,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(Cs_clicks_pct * clicks_7days ), SUM(clicks_7days)) as cs_clicks_pct,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(Cs_actions_pct * actions_7days ), SUM(actions_7days)) as cs_actions_pct,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(Rejection_rate_7days * actions_7days ), SUM(actions_7days)) as Rejection_rate_7days,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(High_risk_url_action_pct * actions_7days ), SUM(actions_7days)) as High_risk_url_action_pct,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(Geo_mismatch_pct * actions_7days ), SUM(actions_7days)) as Geo_mismatch_pct,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(High_risk_login_ip_pct * total_logins_7day ), SUM(total_logins_7day)) as High_risk_login_ip_pct,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(High_risk_login_email_pct * total_logins_7day ), SUM(total_logins_7day)) as High_risk_login_email_pct,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(Abnormal_peak_actions_pct * actions_7days ), SUM(actions_7days)) as Abnormal_peak_actions_pct,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(Abnormal_peak_clicks_pct * clicks_7days ), SUM(clicks_7days)) as Abnormal_peak_clicks_pct,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(Prop_actions_outside * actions_7days ), SUM(actions_7days)) as Prop_actions_outside,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(Prop_clicks_outside * clicks_7days ), SUM(clicks_7days)) as Prop_clicks_outside,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(Prop_actions_no_refurl * actions_7days ), SUM(actions_7days)) as Prop_actions_no_refurl,
       AVG(User_entropy_risk) as avg_user_entropy,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(Rc_proxy_risk * clicks_7days), SUM(clicks_7days)) as Rc_proxy_risk,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(Rc_ip_reputation_risk * clicks_7days), SUM(clicks_7days)) as Rc_ip_reputation_risk,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(Rc_domain_reputation_risk  * clicks_7days), SUM(clicks_7days)) as Rc_domain_reputation_risk ,
       AVG(Final_score) as avg_final_score,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(COUNTIF(risk_level = "critical"), COUNT(*)) as critical_flagged_pct,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(COUNTIF(risk_level = "elevated"), COUNT(*)) as elevated_flagged_pct,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(COUNTIF(risk_level = "mild"), COUNT(*)) as mild_flagged_pct
FROM customers-444618.compliance_agent.partner_continuous_monitoring_final_scores
WHERE DATE(data_date) >= CURRENT_DATE() - INTERVAL @date_interval DAY
  AND publisher_id IN UNNEST(@account_list)
GROUP BY 1, 2, 3;


Step 6: Conditional Detailed Publisher Risk Analysis
Action: Based on the 30-day interval results from Step 5, trigger the following queries. The {interval} or {date_interval} in these queries should be 30 days.
6A: For each account_id where long_cta_pct > 0.1 OR Injected_click_pct > 0.1 OR Click_spamming_pct > 0.1:

SELECT publisher_id, campaign_id,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(actions), SUM(clicks)) as conversion_rate,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(Avg_cta * actions), SUM(actions)) as avg_cta,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(Perc_actions_lt_30sec * actions), SUM(actions)) as Perc_actions_lt_30sec
FROM `customers-444618.compliance_agent.attribution_risk_monitoring_new`
WHERE DATE(data_date) >= CURRENT_DATE() - INTERVAL 30 DAY
  AND publisher_id = @current_account_id
GROUP BY 1, 2;

6B: For account_ids where High_risk_url_action_pct > 0.1:

SELECT publisher_id, domain, SUM(num_actions) as num_actions,
       SUM(IF(rc_url_abnormal_bounce_rate OR rc_url_abnormal_traffic_source OR rc_url_copied_content OR rc_url_low_visit OR rc_url_low_visit_duration OR rc_url_low_word_count, 1, 0) * num_actions) as flagged_actions,
       SUM(IF(rc_url_abnormal_bounce_rate, 1, 0) * num_actions) as rc_url_abnormal_bounce_rate,
       SUM(IF(rc_url_abnormal_traffic_source, 1, 0) * num_actions) as rc_url_abnormal_traffic_source,
       SUM(IF(rc_url_copied_content, 1, 0) * num_actions) as rc_url_copied_content ,
       SUM(IF(rc_url_low_visit, 1, 0) * num_actions) as rc_url_low_visit,
       SUM(IF(rc_url_low_visit_duration, 1, 0) * num_actions) as rc_url_low_visit_duration,
       SUM(IF(rc_url_low_word_count, 1, 0) * num_actions) as rc_url_low_word_count
FROM `customers-444618.compliance_agent.url_risk_monitoring`
WHERE DATE(data_date) >= CURRENT_DATE() - INTERVAL 30 DAY -- Increased from 1 DAY for more context
  AND publisher_id IN UNNEST(@high_risk_url_accounts)
GROUP BY 1, 2
ORDER BY flagged_actions DESC;

6B1: If 6B returns domains with flagged_actions > 0:

SELECT url, traffic_summary_visits, traffic_summary_bounce_rate, traffic_summary_desktop_bounce_rate, traffic_summary_time_on_site, traffic_summary_paid, traffic_summary_referral, traffic_summary_social_paid, traffic_summary_direct, traffic_summary_display_ad, traffic_summary_mail, traffic_summary_search, traffic_summary_social_organic, cs_num_words, cs_best_matched_url, cs_best_matched_pct
FROM `customers-444618.compliance_agent.intelligence_semrush_operator_only`
FULL OUTER JOIN `fq-platform.ds_coe.domain_copyscape_main` ON url = input_domain
WHERE url IN UNNEST(@flagged_domains);

6C: For account_ids where Geo_mismatch_pct > 0.5:

SELECT publisher_id, publisher_name, campaign_id, action_region, publisher_promotional_region, publisher_region, campaign_region, campaign_main_region, campaign_shipping_region, ROUND(SUM(total_actions_7day)/7) as total_actions
FROM `customers-444618.compliance_agent.geo_mismatch_monitoring`
WHERE DATE(data_date) >= CURRENT_DATE() - INTERVAL 30 DAY
  AND publisher_id IN UNNEST(@geo_mismatch_accounts)
GROUP BY 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9
ORDER BY total_actions DESC;

6D: For account_ids where High_risk_login_ip_pct > 0.1:

SELECT account_id, ipaddr, COUNT(*) as logins,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(COUNTIF(high_risk_ip = "yes"), COUNT(*)) as high_risk_logins,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(COUNTIF(rc_ip_bot_activity), COUNT(*)) as bot_activity,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(COUNTIF(rc_ip_crawler), COUNT(*)) as crawler,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(COUNTIF(rc_ip_hosting_provider), COUNT(*)) as hosting_provider,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(COUNTIF(rc_ip_proxy), COUNT(*)) as proxy
FROM `customers-444618.compliance_agent.login_ip_risk_monitoring`
WHERE DATE(data_date) > CURRENT_DATE() - INTERVAL 30 DAY
  AND account_id IN UNNEST(@high_risk_ip_accounts)
GROUP BY 1, 2
ORDER BY logins DESC;

6E: For account_ids where High_risk_login_email_pct > 0.1:

SELECT account_id, email, COUNT(*) as logins,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(COUNTIF(rc_email_disposable), COUNT(*)) as rc_email_disposable,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(COUNTIF(rc_email_domain_risk), COUNT(*)) as rc_email_domain_risk,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(COUNTIF(rc_email_fraud), COUNT(*)) as rc_email_fraud
FROM `customers-444618.compliance_agent.login_email_risk_monitoring`
WHERE DATE(data_date) > CURRENT_DATE() - INTERVAL 30 DAY
  AND account_id IN UNNEST(@high_risk_email_accounts)
GROUP BY 1, 2
ORDER BY logins DESC;

6F: For account_ids where Abnormal_peak_actions_pct > 0.1 or Abnormal_peak_clicks_pct > 0.1:

SELECT publisher_id, campaign_id, actions_ewma6 as expected_actions, num_actions, perc_rise_actions, cam_perc_rise_actions, clicks_ewma6 as expected_clicks, num_clicks, perc_rise_clicks, cam_perc_rise_clicks
FROM `customers-444618.compliance_agent.abnormal_peak_monitoring`
WHERE DATE(data_date) > CURRENT_DATE() - INTERVAL 2 DAY
  AND publisher_id IN UNNEST(@abnormal_peak_accounts)
ORDER BY num_actions DESC;


Step 7: Consolidation
The agent will structure all query results into a nested JSON object, keyed by publisher_id. Each publisher ID will have sub-objects for:
summary: Results from Step 2.1
top_programs: Results from Step 2.2
marketplace_history: Results from Step 3
compliance_history: Results from Step 4
risk_analysis: Containing keys 7D, 30D, 365D for results from Step 5.
detailed_risk: Containing results from any triggered Step 6 queries.
Step 8: Summary Generation (LLM)
The consolidated JSON object is passed to an LLM.
Prompt to LLM: "You are a fraud analyst. Based on the following data, provide a concise summary of the fraud risk for publisher {publisher_ID}, including their links to other accounts, their platform history, compliance issues, key risk indicators from monitoring, and recommended next steps. Reference the JIRA ticket {JIRA_ticket_ID if provided}. Data: {CONSOLIDATED_JSON}"
The LLM generates the natural language output similar to the example provided.
This comprehensive workflow directly uses the provided queries and logic, automates the data gathering and conditional analysis, and leverages an LLM for the final summarization to achieve the desired output.
